[h1]Cosmic Ascendancy[/h1]
[i]The endgame crisis, megastructure, and god-tier progression expansion for the Cosmic Series.[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]🚀 The Ultimate Endgame Experience[/h2]
[b]Cosmic Ascendancy[/b] is the culminating installment of the Cosmic Series. When the Xsotan Wormhole Guardian falls, the galaxy doesn't find peace: it awakens an ancient, ravenous threat, [b]The Eclipse[/b].
Construct massive megastructures, forge god-tier weaponry, and defend the galaxy from apocalyptic World-Eaters in one of the most ambitious endgame crises ever brought to Avorion.

[b]📋 DEPENDENCY:[/b] Cosmic Ascendancy requires [b]Cosmic Vault[/b] and runs standalone from there. It recognizes the other Cosmic mods (Overhaul, War, Chronicles) when they're installed and deepens accordingly, but none of them are required.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Core Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]🔥 [b]The Eclipse Crisis:[/b] A terrifying endgame faction of geometric nightmares. Defeating the Wormhole Guardian awakens them to actively conquer the galaxy map, deploy Lockdown Citadels, and launch devastating Crusades.
[*]☠️ [b]The World-Eater Boss Raid:[/b] Face a colossal 5.9km Juggernaut through a 6-Phase Gauntlet of Quantum EMPs, Gravity Anomalies, Dark Matter Blinks, Anchor Pylons, and Singularity Implosions. Bring friends: the boss scales its Shield, Hull, and damage per defender in the fight.
[*]🎯 [b]Hunt the Dread-Lord:[/b] A wounded Eclipse Nemesis no longer just vanishes when it retreats. It relocates nearby to recover, and `/eclipsestatus` tracks it down so you can finish the job.
[*]🧬 [b]Eclipse Remnant Escalation:[/b] A galaxy that keeps clearing World-Eaters and Citadels doesn't stay easy forever. Confirmed kills build toward five tiers of rising difficulty and a shrinking World-Eater spawn window.
[*]🏛️ [b]The Ascendancy Beacon Megastructure:[/b] Construct a permanent capital checkpoint that stays loaded 24/7. Upgrade it to Tier 5 for permanent, account-wide stat multipliers across your entire fleet, and to Tier 3+ for a Sanctuary Field that actively repels Eclipse expansion nearby.
[*]⚔️ [b]The Stellar Forge:[/b] Extract [i]Ascendant Matter[/i] from fallen Eclipse titans and decrypt Eclipse Datacores to forge custom god-tier weapons and Titan-Class Coaxial Lasers over 24 real-time hours. Claiming a weapon during an active war (with Cosmic War installed) can push its damage multiplier up to a 10.0x cap. Use the [i]Ascendant Scrap[/i] system to guarantee your craft succeeds.
[*]🛡️ [b]Living Relics & Neural Implants:[/b] Equip Ascendant subsystems that dynamically multiply their power based on Core proximity and War Heat. Wire your captain directly into the hull with Neural Implants for god-tier flight and squadron stats.
[*]📖 [b]Epic Story Campaign:[/b] Aegis, the Ascendant Envoy, guides you through a 5-mission campaign (after an initial contact stage) to uncover the origins of The Eclipse, unlock the Ascendancy Forge, and claim [i]The Eclipse Bane[/i] artifact.
[*]💰 [b]The Grand Toll & Economics:[/b] AI factions jumping into your Ascendant capital pay an entry tax (+50% premium from warring factions), granting treasury payouts every 45 minutes. Feed factories Ascendant Matter to activate 3.0x "Ascendant Overdrive."
[*]🚨 [b]Capital Sieges & Citadel Blockades:[/b] Defend your Beacon every 3 to 6 hours from massive invasion fleets to protect your global buffs. Attack Eclipse Citadels that physically trap players in the sector with hyperspace suppression fields.
[*]🗺️ [b]Faction AI 4X-Style Expansion & Fallen Empires:[/b] AI factions and Pirates organically expand their borders and claim uncharted sectors. If The Eclipse annihilates 75 sectors, it triggers a "Fallen Empire" state and systematically wipes out AI faction capitals.
[*]🌑 [b]The Dark Sector & Rift Hazards:[/b] Uncharted sectors near the Galactic Core carry up to a 50% chance of dropping you into permanent Dark Matter Fog fields crawling with Eclipse Juggernauts and Rift Spillage hazards.
[*]📊 [b]The Eclipse Threat Dashboard:[/b] `/eclipsestatus` reports the full picture: total territory held, expansion threat, Fallen Empire status, a wounded Nemesis's last known position, and your current Remnant Tier.
[*]📰 [b]Galactic Dread News:[/b] Server-wide breaking news whenever The Eclipse annihilates a sector or players secure a heroic victory against an Obliterator or World-Eater.
[/list]

